# Assets the game loads

The game is a static web page (`index.html` + `src/`, no build step). It loads
every asset below from the `assets/` directory at the delivery root, which the
`artist` position supplies. Paths are case-sensitive. If a file is missing the
game falls back to plain shapes/colours and stays playable, so missing assets
never break a build — but the shipped game should have all of them.

Grid: 20 x 20 cells, each cell drawn at 32 x 32 px (canvas 640 x 640).

## Images (PNG, RGBA, transparent background unless stated)

| Path | Size (px) | What it shows |
|---|---|---|
| `assets/images/snake_head.png` | 32 x 32 | Snake head **facing right** (moving right). The game rotates it for up/down/left. |
| `assets/images/snake_body.png` | 32 x 32 | One straight body segment, **horizontal** (game rotates for vertical). Should tile seamlessly left-to-right with itself, the head and the tail. |
| `assets/images/snake_tail.png` | 32 x 32 | Tail end, **pointing left** (the rest of the snake is to its right). Game rotates it. |
| `assets/images/food.png` | 32 x 32 | The food item (e.g. an apple), centred, ~24 px visible. |
| `assets/images/tile.png` | 32 x 32 | Opaque floor tile drawn under every grid cell. Subtle, low contrast so snake and food read clearly. |
| `assets/images/title.png` | 512 x 160 | "SNAKE" title logo for the title screen, transparent background. |

## Audio (MP3, mono or stereo, 44.1 kHz, short, normalised, no leading silence)

| Path | Length | When it plays |
|---|---|---|
| `assets/audio/eat.mp3` | < 0.3 s | Snake eats food. |
| `assets/audio/game_over.mp3` | < 1.5 s | Snake hits a wall or itself. |
| `assets/audio/start.mp3` | < 0.8 s | Player starts / restarts a game. |

## Theme

`assets/theme.json` — colours and font for the screens and HUD, so the UI
matches the art:

```json
{
  "background": "#101820",
  "text": "#f0f0e0",
  "accent": "#7bd36b",
  "danger": "#e0533b",
  "font": "\"Press Start 2P\", monospace"
}
```

All keys optional; the game uses the defaults above for any missing key. If
`font` names a web font, put the font file under `assets/fonts/` and add
`"fontFile": "assets/fonts/<file>"` (woff2 or ttf); the game loads it.
